========================================
1. Backward Incompatible Changes
========================================

- Curl:
  . curl_multi_exec() now throws a TypeError when still_running is not an int.

- PDO:
  . PDOStatement::bindColumn() now throws a ValueError when the column name is
    not present in the result set. It previously reported the condition
    through PDO::ATTR_ERRMODE and returned false.

- Standard:
  . The number of filters that can be chained in a php://filter URL is limited
    to 16 by default. Set the stream context option max_filter_count to change
    this.
  . On Unix systems, proc_close() now reports termination by a signal as
    128 + the signal number, following the shell convention, instead of the
    raw wait status (e.g. 137 instead of 9 for SIGKILL). This also applies when
    proc_get_status() observed the termination first; previously proc_close()
    returned -1 in that case. Normal exit codes are unchanged.
  . On Unix systems, proc_get_status() now also caches the status of a child
    terminated by a signal, as it does for normal exits since PHP 8.3.
    Repeated calls keep reporting "signaled" => true and the "termsig" value,
    and "cached" is true. Previously, calls after the first one reported
    "signaled" => false and "termsig" => 0.

========================================
2. New Features
========================================

- Intl:
  . Locale::acceptFromHttp() and locale_accept_from_http() now accept an
    optional $availableLocales array argument. When given, the
    Accept-Language header is matched against these locales instead of all
    locales known to ICU, and the matching entry is returned as passed.
    A ValueError is thrown if the array is empty or contains an invalid
    locale, and a TypeError if it contains a non-string value.

- Streams:
  . The so_linger, so_rcvbuf and so_sndbuf stream socket context options are
    now also applied to unix and unix datagram sockets.

